## Problem Statement

The current `Chalk::IR::Node` implementation uses a generic node class with an `op` field and dispatch tables throughout the codebase. This creates several maintenance issues:

1. **Giant dispatch tables** - Every component (Builder, Validator, future Interpreter/CodeGen) has large `given ($node->op)` switch statements
2. **Scattered logic** - Node-specific behavior is spread across multiple files instead of being encapsulated
3. **Error-prone** - Adding a new node type requires updating 4-5 different dispatch tables
4. **No polymorphism** - Can't leverage Perl's OOP for cleaner code

**Current architecture:**
```perl
# lib/Chalk/IR/Node.pm - generic node with op field
class Chalk::IR::Node {
    field $op :param;
    field $attributes :param;
    # ... all nodes share this class
}

# lib/Chalk/IR/Validator.pm - giant dispatch table
method validate_all($graph) {
    given ($node->op) {
        when ('Constant') { ... }
        when ('Add') { ... }
        when ('Store') { ... }
        # 30+ more cases
    }
}

# lib/Chalk/IR/Builder.pm - giant dispatch table
method peephole($graph) {
    given ($op) {
        when ('Add') { ... }
        when ('Multiply') { ... }
        # repeated everywhere
    }
}
```

## Proposed Solution

Refactor into a polymorphic class hierarchy where each node type is a subclass with its own behavior:

```perl
# Base class
class Chalk::IR::Node {
    field $id :param :reader;
    field $inputs :param :reader;
    field $graph :param :reader = undef;

    # Polymorphic interface
    method execute($env) { die "Abstract" }
    method validate($validator) { return () }
    method optimize() { return $self }
    method op() { die "Abstract" }
    method to_hash() { ... }
}

# Concrete node types
class Chalk::IR::Node::Constant :isa(Chalk::IR::Node) {
    field $value :param :reader;
    field $type :param :reader = 'Int';

    method op() { 'Constant' }
    method execute($env) { return $value }
    method optimize() { return $self }  # Constants don't optimize
}

class Chalk::IR::Node::Add :isa(Chalk::IR::Node) {
    field $left :param :reader;   # NodeRef
    field $right :param :reader;  # NodeRef

    method op() { 'Add' }

    method execute($env) {
        my $l = $graph->get_node($left->{node_id})->execute($env);
        my $r = $graph->get_node($right->{node_id})->execute($env);
        return $l + $r;
    }

    method optimize() {
        # Constant folding logic here
        my $l_node = $graph->get_node($left->{node_id});
        my $r_node = $graph->get_node($right->{node_id});

        if ($l_node->op eq 'Constant' && $r_node->op eq 'Constant') {
            return Chalk::IR::Node::Constant->new(
                id => $self->id,
                inputs => $self->inputs,
                value => $l_node->value + $r_node->value,
                graph => $graph
            );
        }
        return $self;
    }

    method validate($validator) {
        my @errors;
        # Add-specific validation
        unless ($graph->get_node($left->{node_id})) {
            push @errors, "Add node $id references invalid left operand";
        }
        return @errors;
    }
}
```

