Perfect! Now I understand. `SPPFViterbiSemiring` is implemented as a composite (SPPF + Viterbi) on lines 180-187.

So for `--generate-ir`, we need to create a similar composite but with SPPF + Semantic instead of SPPF + Viterbi.

The fix for `app.pl` in `--generate-ir` mode (starting at line 223) should be:

```perl
# Create IR Builder
my $builder = Chalk::IR::Builder->new();

# Create SPPF semiring
my $sppf_sr = Chalk::Semiring::SPPF->new();

# Create Semantic semiring with Builder in environment
my $semantic_sr = Chalk::Semiring::Semantic->new(
    grammar => $chalk_grammar,
    env => { ir_builder => $builder }
);

# Create composite semiring (SPPF + Semantic)
my $composite = Chalk::Semiring::Composite->new(
    semirings => [$sppf_sr, $semantic_sr]
);

# Create parser with composite semiring
my $parser = Chalk::Parser->new(
    grammar => $chalk_grammar,
    semiring => $composite,  # NOT just SPPFViterbiSemiring!
    preprocess => $preprocess
);
```

Then after parsing, extract the IR graph from the builder:
```perl
my $graph = $builder->graph;
```

So you're right - we should be using a composite semiring. The issue is that `--generate-ir` uses the wrong composite (SPPF+Viterbi) instead of creating a new composite (SPPF+Semantic).

