## Expected Behavior

Running `perl app.pl --generate-ir` should:
1. Discover all Chalk modules in lib/ using File::Find
2. Parse each file with Chalk grammar using Semantic semiring
3. Extract IR graphs from semantic actions
4. Validate each IR graph using Chalk::IR::Validator
5. Collect and report statistics (files processed, nodes generated, validation errors)
6. Support output formats: text (default), json, dot (via --output-format flag)

## Implementation Location

File: `app.pl` around line 100 (after grammar loading, before main execution)

## Pseudo-code

```perl
if ($generate_ir_mode) {
    use File::Find;
    use Chalk::IR::Validator;
    use Chalk::Semiring::Semantic;

    my @modules;
    find(sub {
        push @modules, $File::Find::name if /\.pm$/ && -f;
    }, 'lib/Chalk');

    my ($passed, $failed) = (0, 0);
    my @errors;

    for my $file (sort @modules) {
        my $content = read_file($file);
        my $parser = Chalk::Parser->new(
            grammar => $chalk_grammar,
            semiring => 'Semantic'
        );

        my $result = $parser->parse_string($content);
        if ($result && $result->{graph}) {
            my $validator = Chalk::IR::Validator->new();
            my @validation_errors = $validator->validate($result->{graph});

            if (@validation_errors) {
                $failed++;
                push @errors, { file => $file, errors => \@validation_errors };
            } else {
                $passed++;
            }

            output_graph($result->{graph}, $file, $output_format);
        } else {
            $failed++;
            push @errors, { file => $file, errors => ['Parse failed'] };
        }
    }

    print_summary($passed, $failed, \@errors, $output_format);
    exit($failed > 0 ? 1 : 0);
}
```

